WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:08.400
During the war of independence,
the space pirates banded together just once

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.880
to overcome their overseer, the Stellar Alliance.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.990
The pirate's song, which signaled a meeting,

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.370
has been unleashed upon space again.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.200
The path has opened.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.870
But if they cannot overcome the danger facing them,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.210
they will never know what awaits.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.650
What will happen?

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.970
If you want a fight, you've got one!

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.620
Unbelievable pressure.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.700
Is that all coming from one battleship?

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.210
Sorry, I can't get ahead of them.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.710
I'm trying hard just to keep them at bay!

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.340
At least it's preventing them from hitting us!

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.800
Keep it up!

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.180
Roger!

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:47.980
Things haven't been this bad since we dropped out of warp amidst the Empire's seventh fleet.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.560
Okay, back on line.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.190
The Bentenmaru is to maintain distance from the enemy and head to 10:00 portside!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.400
Roger.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.820
Turning to port.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.700
Gravity waves.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.120
Not that big yet.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.120
The ship is maintaining standard navigation as it bears toward us.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.700
What do we do?

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.290
It's one against one.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.620
But they have the firepower equivalent of a whole fleet.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.670
And they can zigzag toward us.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.300
Pirates don't pick fights they can't win.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.010
You want to run?

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:21.220
At this range, they'll shoot us from behind.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.440
We'll get enough distance for an FTL jump.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.770
Right now, we're just staring each other down.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.900
Our chance will come when they
come at us with their gravity.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.530
Where will we touch down?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.320
Within the shortest distance possible,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.870
but change our navigation route so they can't follow us.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:48.950
Roger.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.290
What about counterattacks?

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.460
Just enough to keep them from figuring out our plan.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.540
Hold some back for the very last minute.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.630
Roger.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.380
You know what to do with the sensors, right?

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.800
Yup.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.550
What do you think of Marika as a captain now?

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.800
She's gotten pretty good.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:04.470
San-Daime!

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.600
I know!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.720
If we survive, I'll have to let her know.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.690
Commencing attack.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.220
What's wrong?

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.160
Not going to advance?

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.830
If you won't come to us,
how about we entice you?

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.540
Turn us around!

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.500
The Bentenmaru will turn tail and run!

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:44.680
If they won't strike, then we run at full speed and follow with an FTL jump!

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.550
And if they do?

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.550
We spin back around.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:51.640
If they zigzag at us, we take them head-on.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.230
We'll give them a kick before they're on top of us!

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.060
Give them a kick?

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.650
Pretty funny, Captain.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.270
Kane, take care of it.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.480
Right.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:06.160
Ready those FTL coordinates.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.660
I'll fire the main cannon here.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.710
Gunners and crew, take positions where the armor is thickest.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.670
If you're in the wrong place during a frontal assault, you'll get dragged out through a hole.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.300
Gravity wave sensors are still maxed out.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.430
I'll try calculating the enemy's route.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.100
Sorry, we might be betting on luck.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.890
Bentenmaru, here we go!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:04.630
There it is!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.550
Just like we saw with the Big Catch.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.640
It charges to max, and seven seconds later, here they come.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.640
Change course! 180-degree spin!

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.100
Roger!

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:32.410
If it happens the same way as before, they'll reach the Bentenmaru in fifteen seconds.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.040
<i>What is this?</i>

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.290
<i>It's as fast as a fighter.</i>

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.420
<i>Fighters don't zigzag!</i>

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.710
Don't let them get above us!

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.470
Doing what I can!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.930
Get as many dispersers out there as you can!

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.680
Hang in there, engines!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.440
Strike to upper armor plate!

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.490
Begin counterattack!

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.700
With everything we have!

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.320
Firing main cannon.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.920
The Bentenmaru is getting riddled with holes!

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.130
Maximum acceleration!
Take us out of here!

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:27.460
Roger!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:32.300
We're gonna hit them!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.800
The hell we will!

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:50.440
The enemy's decelerating, but still maintaining course.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.740
They're heading away from the Bentenmaru.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.450
What about their gravity waves?

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.700
Minimal.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.120
We're safe.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:01.750
How bad is the damage?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:02.960
Can we jump?

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.130
We're repairing the damaged areas.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:09.800
As soon as that's done, we can probably manage one jump.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.170
Got it.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.470
Prepare for FTL jump.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:22.980
That fight was from closer range than anything previously.

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.940
Crossing paths in the vast depths of space...

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.820
It's not romantic at all.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:28.860
It's nuts.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.320
Nice job, me.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.490
Are you going to compliment me?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:41.540
I suppose.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.970
Incoming message.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.020
It's from the space pirate ship Barbalusa.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:05.520
My dad?

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.480
Put it through.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.610
There you are, Captain Marika.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:12.360
Seems the Bentenmaru took some damage.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.900
Yeah, just a little.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:20.330
How was your trip with your favorite captain, Chiaki?

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.500
Was it fun?

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.330
Dad, you jerk! What are you saying?

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.960
That's the pirate's nest, isn't it?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.380
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.020
The
Safety
Repairs

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.200
We sustained some real damage.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.370
This isn't the time to be impressed.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.620
While we're fixing it, let's make some upgrades.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.670
We've been making a lot lately.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:14.210
Oh, I just got a message from the captain about that.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.050
I get it. So that's her plan.

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:25.390
Our captain has some interesting ideas.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.730
Okay, I'm in.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.060
Send it to our lady on the outside.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.520
Our lady, huh?

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.500
Wow!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:59.970
I heard that you could introduce me to repair crews and merchants around here.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.050
I need to repair a spaceship.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.430
Show me what you've got.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.140
S-Sure.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.900
But it'll cost you.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.860
I imagine it will.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.980
We're a made-to-order pirate ship.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:21.030
A-Are you with the Benten...

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.490
You have got sharp eyes.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.990
So perhaps you really can help me.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.960
Make out the invoice to the Bentenmaru.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:50.600
What's up?

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.020
Come to the infirmary.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.690
Give me a sec.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.690
Coorie, you there?

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:01.030
Yeah, I am. Got it.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.490
Okay, I'll leave the rest to San-Daime.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.870
Have that update ready.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.280
Roger.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.330
It really is a waste.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.500
You should dress like that all the time.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.250
Nope. Definitely not.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.210
Right, right.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:21.260
But aren't you playing with the
comms systems a little too much?

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.930
Is that Hyakume's plan?

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.470
No, this was the captain's order.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.560
When it's done, we'll be able to command a fleet.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.430
It looks fun.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:41.690
Doctor, it's Luca.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.150
That's unusual.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.320
Come in.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.200
It's about Kane.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.370
Kane?

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:59.630
Thanks to you, everyone's heard the pirate's song.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:04.010
Currently, the pirate ships here are my Barbalusa,

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.260
your Bentenmaru,

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.760
Kachua's Viracocha,

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.520
Witherspoon's El Santo.

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:18.810
And many other pirate ships are en route as well.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.280
Touchdown in front of us.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.030
Impossible! I don't believe it!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.660
What's wrong? Report!

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.280
There's something approaching!

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.410
It's zig-zagging! And it's fast!

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.870
It's them! Prepare for combat!

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.970
John's Southern Island was lost.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.640
Several other ships have also been downed.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:59.190
We may not even get ten.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.820
Well, that's how it is.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:08.280
When they set their course for the pirate's nest, the rest was up to them.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.570
No one blames you.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:15.040
It'll take three days for the rest
to get to the pirate's nest.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:18.040
Have the Bentenmaru repaired by then.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.040
We've got lots to do, right?

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.510
You're right.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:29.720
Ready?

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.800
Yeah, thanks, chef.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.470
I'm starving.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.350
My younger brother told me about you.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.070
You appear to be doing well.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.650
Your brother?

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.280
That old man's...

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.570
I'm his older brother.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.570
There are five of us.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.820
We each have our own restaurants.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:52.950
A chain?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.160
Something like that.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.330
I'll bring you some delicious food!

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:03.040
His meals are wonderful.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.300
He's everything you'd expect
from the legendary chef's son.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.510
So the chef has a brother.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:11.760
There are five of them, huh?

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.680
I wonder what the other three are called.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.600
Chef? Cook?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:18.980
Master?

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.980
That's irrelevant.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.350
Yeah.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.230
It doesn't matter.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.440
The food was good.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:32.610
What will you do about the Pirate's Council?

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.330
Well, it'll work out.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.540
You have a plan, right?
I can tell by your face.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.400
These are veteran pirates.
How will you deal with them?

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.170
Just watch.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.300
Then I'll look forward to seeing it.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.590
Kato Marika, captain of the Bentenmaru, being a pirate.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.590
See you later.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.550
Thanks for walking with me.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.930
The space warship Grand Cross.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:44.810
Its full designation is the Mobile Battleship Grand Cross, Alpha Prototype.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.230
I am Captain Quartz Christie.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.650
A captain from where?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:49.780
The Galactic Empire?

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.320
It's someone's experimental ship.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.110
That should suffice.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.620
A new weapon?

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:57.870
No comment.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.370
I see.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.750
Just as the report said.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.540
Coming here was worth it.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:10.300
The first pirate ship to escape the Grand Cross...

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:13.510
Captain of the Bentenmaru, Kato Marika.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:16.010
Why are you attacking pirates?

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.260
Just because.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.720
They're good experimental subjects.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.430
What do you think of the pirates in this region?

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:29.400
They just keep renewing their old Letters of Marque.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:34.440
And they don't use them for anything but putting on little shows.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.280
They're no longer pirates.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:39.120
They're not needed at all.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.660
And if they're not needed, no one will care if they're gone, right?

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.450
That's all it is.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.040
I'll care.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.000
And everyone else will too.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.920
So we'll fight.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.550
Fight, then.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.970
And don't let me down.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.300
Stealth?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.140
Below?

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:04.770
Let's go!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.020
Use the therm-sensors.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.940
Contact station security.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:10.730
Roger.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:13.650
Are you all right?

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.570
She said, "Just as the report said."

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.200
I guess we do have a spy after all.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.910
I have already taken measures.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:54.020
Isn't it about time for you to come out?

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.070
How long have you known?

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.160
The whole time.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.580
You're way too obvious.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.660
But I learned a lot.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:06.420
Misa!

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.880
What are you doing?

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.090
I thought something was strange.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:17.260
But revealing yourself has helped.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.060
W-Why?

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.110
That was the proof.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.780
Any Luca who can talk with a
hole in her head isn't Luca.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.070
Who are you?

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.370
Androids these days are pretty well made.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:52.370
You're the one who's been relaying the Bentenmaru's course.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.720
When did you realize?

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:11.520
When Luca ratted you out.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:17.290
Luca doesn't care about anything except her work.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:19.610
Luca caring about something
else was very suspicious.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:23.240
Your turn.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.160
ID data confirmed.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.200
That's the real Kane. No doubt about it.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.210
You're hiding things too.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:38.130
If they will hurt the Bentenmaru...

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.420
It's fine. I know.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.180
Where are you, Ririka?

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:55.810
After leaving the sea resort planet, I boarded a luxury liner.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.520
Space is great.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.690
The stars shine so prettily.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.320
I wish I were that lucky.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.190
Over here, our ship's in rough shape.

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.900
It's getting repairs galore.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:06.950
Well, keep at it.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:09.200
If you earn some money, you can have fun.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.120
Right now, the repairs are costing tons out of pocket.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.000
Oh, right.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.250
Your school.

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:19.630
You won't be there for a while, right?

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:22.880
I notified them that you'd be out for two weeks.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:26.550
Oh, I forgot! Thanks, Ririka.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:29.010
Are you gonna pass this year?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:31.720
My attendance will be pretty close.

